    "created_at": "2016-11-30T13:46:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-30T13:46:31Z",
    "body": "Just a quick thought: when a website goes fullscreen then browsers display a notification that informs the user about this, to prevent phishing attacks. Wouldn't it be possible to implement a similar mechanism for the noopener issue? This would maintain backwards compatibility, and allows for a secure mechanism without notification to be implemented in parallel. ",
